Snapshot 2026-09-25 (i265): eob from the inverse scan, and C's cul-level form.

Cell: 1024x1024 gradient qp40 p10 still (the perf_2026-09-25-gap cell).
A line-level profile put 8M Ir of tx_unit_inner's 18.3M self cost in
`quant::eob_from_qcoeff`: a reverse scan-order walk, one scattered load per
position, the whole block for an all-zero one. C's AVX2 quantizers get eob
as a raster max over `iscan`.

- gen_scan_tables now also emits the inverse scans (computed at compile time
  by a const fn from the scan statics) with `iscan()` and `iscan_for(scan)`
  (identity lookup among the tables of that length); scan_tables.rs is
  regenerated (the scan data is unchanged).
- `svtav1_dsp::quant_coding::eob_from_iscan`: a `#[magetypes]` i32x8 kernel
  (v3, neon, scalar). `eob_from_qcoeff` uses it for every generated scan and
  keeps the walk (`eob_by_walk`) for any other slice.
- tx_unit_inner computes cul_level in C's form (scan[0..eob], early exit)
  when eob <= n/8, the raster sum otherwise.
- Tests: iscan eob == reverse walk for all 57 scans on zero, single and
  random blocks under every dispatch tier; both cul-level forms agree.

output: byte-identical (.obu cmp; perf_ab ident=Y; nextest 2769/2769 with
        pins unchanged; spotcheck 147/147)

callgrind Ir, 1024 p10: 329,726,815 -> 319,646,721 (-3.06%)
  eob: 5.57M (walk, outlined) -> 3.16M kernel + 1.16M iscan_for
  tx_unit_inner self: 18.29M -> 7.44M

